  teen: ['Ages 12–17: how to train right', [['p', 'WHO recommends that young people aged 5–17 do moderate-to-vigorous activity for **an average of 60 minutes a day**, including muscle- and bone-strengthening 3 times a week.'], ['li', ['Light, supervised strength training is safe and **does not stunt growth** – what matters is good technique.', 'No strict calorie cutting; eat full meals with enough milk and protein.', 'Limit recreational screen time and sleep 8–10 hours.', 'Talk to your parents or teachers if you worry about your weight or looks.']]]],
